+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a category currently cascades into deleting products that are assigned only to that category, which breaks inventory, carts, and historical orders. The category tree and its product associations need to be removed without deleting the products or making existing commerce records unreadable.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make private category deletion remove only the selected category, its descendants, and their product-category associations.
+- Preserve every affected product, including inventory, pricing, and associations with categories outside the deleted subtree.
+- Return HTTP 404 when the requested category does not exist, and make deleted categories and their product listings unavailable through the public APIs.
+- Add regression coverage for descendant deletion, product preservation, 404 behavior, and cart/order continuity.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `category-deletion`: Define safe recursive category deletion and its observable API behavior.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The category service and private category REST endpoint are affected, along with product-category persistence and integration tests covering products, carts, orders, and public category APIs. No product, inventory, cart, or order domain model should be deleted or rewritten as part of category removal.
